-## 12. Expected milestone decision
-
-V557 can end in four honest states:
-
-1. The V556 corpus lacks a historical label commitment. Retire that lineage
-   and preserve its raw bytes only as non-held development evidence.
-2. The exact record has backend parity, but scalar energy gives no held final-
-   decision gain. Preserve the null and retain the record as verification
-   infrastructure.
-3. The production-shadow learner improves future exact yield across domains
-   without retention or lifecycle failure. Promote only that bounded external-
-   memory result.
-4. The live ARC shield prevents a held safety regression but does not improve
-   mean reachability. Promote it only as a default-off safety fallback.
-
-The milestone succeeds if it produces trustworthy, independently recomputable
-determinations. Positive effects are not required.
+| Exp6480-6481 | research operations and infrastructure | REQ-INFRA-6480 through REQ-INFRA-6481 |
+| Exp6482-6486 | verification and verifiable reasoning | REQ-VERIFY-6482 through REQ-VERIFY-6486 |
+| Exp6487-6489 | continuous learning | REQ-LEARN-6487 through REQ-LEARN-6489 |
+| Exp6490-6491 | ARC-AGI live path | REQ-ARC-6490 through REQ-ARC-6491 |
+| Exp6492 | research reporting | REQ-REPORT-6492 |
+
+Each requirement needs at least one SCENARIO entry, implementation evidence,
+focused tests, and traceability reconciliation. A task must read the applicable
+E2E plan before it declares completion.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+The milestone is complete when:
+
+1. All 13 task IDs have terminal artifacts or explicit blocked artifacts.
+2. The Exp6463 lineage is not used as held evidence.
+3. Any new LLM task includes at least one mandated SOTA GGUF. Exp6483 includes
+   all three.
+4. Every comparative claim has per-unit rows and row-derived aggregates.
+5. Exp6487 executes a chronological continuous self-learning protocol.
+6. Every persistent cache write has exact pre-admission evidence.
+7. Every CSL transition claim clears a measured frozen null.
+8. ARC work uses the reachable live path, includes registry precheck, records
+   solve_provenance, and makes no targeted solve claim.
+9. No learned signal becomes release authority.
+10. No hardware claim is made without authenticated execution evidence.
+11. Focused tests, spec coverage, row-consistency lint, adversarial verification,
+    and applicable E2E checks are recorded.
+12. OpenSpec, traceability, status, and changelog are reconciled without editing
+    public results or the conductor.
+
+## Claim boundaries
+
+V558 may claim:
+
+- prospective exact-energy selection on the measured local-SOTA stream, if its
+  held gates pass;
+- a bounded equal-budget allocation result, if Exp6485 runs;
+- guarded factor-cache continuous learning, if Exp6489 grants eligibility;
+- ARC decision-metric or executed-policy effects on the measured game-blind
+  roster, if the relevant gates pass.
+
+V558 may not claim:
+
+- a global EBM reasoning theorem;
+- a repaired or valid Exp6463 held result;
+- learned-score release authority;
+- semantic correctness from format validity;
+- a new ARC game or level solve as the task objective;
+- Kona, Extropic, FPGA, TSU, or other hardware execution;
+- public leaderboard or paper changes.
+
+## Decentralization implications
+
+The milestone uses local open-weight GGUF models, local exact solvers, and local
+event ledgers. It does not require a hosted judge, proprietary verifier, remote
+memory service, or unavailable accelerator. Raw outputs and exact decisions
+remain replayable on operator-controlled hardware.
+
+The architecture also narrows trust. A model can propose. A cache can remember.
+An energy can rank. Only a local exact checker can admit a write or release a
+decision. This separation keeps the useful adaptive layer replaceable and
+auditable without centralizing authority in one model provider or one hardware
+vendor.
+
+## Explicit non-goals
+
+- Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml.
+- Do not modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
+- Do not push.
+- Do not reopen finite-ID generation, grammar repair, external-text scoring,
+  hidden-state scoring, the Exp6463 corpus, or a retired ARC patch.
+- Do not train a new KAN or EBT.
+- Do not probe unchanged FPGA or thermodynamic hardware.
+- Do not modify public results or publication surfaces.
